# N6 Display Preparation

Scope: STEMROBIN-182 / 182-6 / book `8a` / `modern-us-neutral` /
`alg8-c1-s2-n6`. This sidecar owns only its directory and the adjacent
`.tmp/resume182-6-8a-n6-select3695.mjs`. Nothing here is content approval,
application acceptance or final integration.

Preparation and syntax checks do not run the renderer, browser or selector.
Imported source bytes are retained once, never imported or executed. Existing
renderer modules and existing linked project dependencies are hash-pinned.
`preparation-FIRST-failure.record` retains the preparation-only dependency-link
diagnosis. No earlier evidence or screenshots were copied.

## Parent Commands

All commands run from:
`/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/stemrobin-182-six-3695/lemmadeck`.

Check prepared inputs without reserving FIRST or launching any engine:

```sh
node .tmp/resume182-6-8a-n6-display3695-FIRST/run.mjs --check-inputs
```

After prepared inputs, execute FIRST once:

```sh
node .tmp/resume182-6-8a-n6-display3695-FIRST/run.mjs --first --wait-seconds 1800
```

The wait is only for missing retained dependencies or draft answer status.
Invalid identity, changed pins or failed audits stop the dependent stages.
No parent approval token, backend call, environment file or extra validator
is required.

After runtime success, derive the minimal visual observation set:

```sh
node .tmp/resume182-6-8a-n6-select3695.mjs --report /Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/stemrobin-182-six-3695/lemmadeck/.tmp/resume182-6-8a-n6-display3695-FIRST/runtime-FIRST/report-FIRST.json --name first
```

Recover only a failed display transaction whose renderer and HTML already passed:

```sh
node .tmp/resume182-6-8a-n6-display3695-FIRST/run.mjs --recover correction1 --from /Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/stemrobin-182-six-3695/lemmadeck/.tmp/resume182-6-8a-n6-display3695-FIRST/runtime-FIRST/report-FIRST.json
```

Recovery verifies unchanged input/staged/HTML/screenshot hashes and stable target
IDs. It runs no renderer, skips completed views, and reuses passed screenshots
within an incomplete view. The original failure/report and every screenshot stay
in place. Use a new recovery name, and pass its report to a newly named selection.
A renderer failure is not recoverable through this browser-only path.

## Preconditions

Pinned: current ready lesson/exercises/figures, PASS adaptation audit, current
PASS hash-bound fig-09/10/11/12 assets/specs/reviews/render receipts, renderer
modules and existing dependency entrypoints. This reuses those reviews, not
source/math/figure re-review.

Must exist in this lesson directory:

- `choice-set/seed.json`, `choice-set/draft.json`, `choice-set/review.json`:
  current lesson/book, current exercise/concept/figure projections, current trace,
  canonical seed/draft hashes and PASS review.
- Any used choice assets must already be retained below this lesson's
  `choice-set/figures/` with their existing hash-bound PASS reviews.
- `answer-keys.json`: ready, current book/edition/lesson, all 12 exercise IDs and
  exact current prompts.
- `answer-keys.audit.json`: current lesson-audit schema, PASS, matching count.

## Evidence

FIRST writes `runtime-FIRST/`; recovery writes `runtime-recovery-<name>/`.
Each contains runtime report, events, usage, DOM target inventories, exact
native-viewport coverage, all screenshot receipts and visual handoff. FIRST
also retains the scratch-only relocated public choice views and all three
project-rendered HTML files. Private answer/key/intent data is not served.

Desktop 1440x960 and mobile 390x844 use isolated headless Chromium, localhost
HTML only, inline existing fonts/assets, no persistent profile or OS interaction.
Each actual text glyph, math glyph/rule, SVG label and complete media region must
be reachable and covered. HTML Range fontbox allowance remains the inherited
0.5px; painted math rules, SVG geometry/labels and media region boundaries have
zero allowance. Scroll corrections round inward with ceil. Subparts compare
against the preceding nonempty line.

The selector hashes bytes but does not observe images. It uses actual glyph/rule/
media target IDs and partitions figure regions by all captured rectangle edges,
then applies greedy set cover and removes redundancy, proving inclusion
minimality with indispensable-target witnesses. It does not claim a globally
minimum cardinality solution. Failed/redundant captures remain saved and are
never marked reviewed.

Only `RUNTIME_PASS_VISUAL_PENDING` is possible at runtime success. Fresh bounded
reviewers inspect the selected batches (at most eight new images per batch,
24 per context), return actual observed paths/hashes, and stop. Parent owns
observations and final binding.
